# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Both keys are the same Anthropic key; they
# differ in WHERE they are read, which is the whole point.

# Server-side, used by the proxy in api/claude.ts. This is the one that matters
# in production: the browser never sees it, because every AI call goes through
# the proxy, which rebuilds the request from a whitelist before forwarding it.
#
# Set a spend cap on the key in the Anthropic Console. That is the real backstop
# against abuse — the proxy's rate limiter is per serverless instance and in
# memory, so it is a speed bump rather than a cap.
#
# Use a key scoped to THIS app. Sharing one key across projects means one app's
# traffic can exhaust the other's budget, and neither can be revoked alone.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# DEV ONLY. `services/claudeService.ts` attaches this for direct browser calls
# when `import.meta.env.DEV` is true, so the app works with `npm run dev` before
# a proxy is running locally.
#
# It is NOT a production leak: Vite replaces `import.meta.env.DEV` with `false`
# at build time and tree-shakes the branch. Verified by grepping the built
# bundle — neither this variable name nor any `sk-ant-` material appears in
# `dist/`. Do not set it in Vercel.
VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
